{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task. This is the foundational question for a multimodal cellular profiling study: if image has no discriminative power, all multimodal configurations lose their main rationale. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides a clean, controlled comparison to config_001—both use singleprofile with no aggregation—so any performance difference is attributable to the modality itself rather than to profile setting or aggregation. ResNet50 is chosen as the standard, well-calibrated image encoder baseline before exploring ViT-L. This experiment reduces the largest source of uncertainty (modality-level signal) and directly informs whether to invest subsequent budget in multimodal fusion or to focus on improving the RNA side (e.g., better encoders or multiprofile aggregation)."
}

